{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0119XmyQEHa4nCmzon2rFokX","type":"tool_result","content":"50\t\tBundleDigest    string `json:\"bundle_digest\"`\n51\t\tDigest          string `json:\"digest\"`\n52\t\tText            string `json:\"text\"`\n53\t}\n54\t\n55\t// The review template that briefs rounds and asks for a pose-draft block\n56\t// (spec pose-delegated-review-round-protocol), and the one before it, kept so\n57\t// a run briefed with it still verifies.\n58\tconst (\n59\t\t// A change to the text of a published version takes a new one (spec\n60\t\t// pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable). /5 stated how a round after the first\n61\t\t// names the findings it accounts for.\n62\t\treviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs = \"review-brief/5\"\n63\t\t// reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules stated the accepted-risk severities and more, see briefRulesText.\n64\t\treviewBriefTemplateRiskRules = \"review-brief/6\"\n65\t\t// reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable is the current template: it also says that a draft\n66\t\t// cannot dispense with every required criterion as not-applicable.\n67\t\treviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable = \"review-brief/7\"\n68\t\t// reviewBriefTemplateConclusions asked for the typed conclusion and stated its rules,\n69\t\t// without the identifiers of the findings of earlier rounds.\n70\t\t// reviewBriefTemplateConclusions (/4) asked for the typed conclusion and stated the rules\n71\t\t// the engine checks before it records one (spec pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules).\n72\t\treviewBriefTemplateConclusions = \"review-brief/4\"\n73\t\t// reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion asked for the conclusion without stating\n74\t\t// those rules; kept so a run briefed with it still verifies and concludes.\n75\t\treviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion = \"review-brief/3\"\n76\t\treviewBriefTemplateRounds          = \"review-brief/2\"\n77\t\treviewBriefTemplateFirst           = \"review-brief/1\"\n78\t)\n79\t\n80\t// reviewBriefAsksConclusion reports a template that asks for the typed conclusion.\n81\tfunc reviewBriefAsksConclusion(template string) bool {\n82\t\treturn template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable || template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || template == reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs || template == reviewBriefTemplateConclusions || template == reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion\n83\t}\n84\t\n85\t// briefRulesTextV5 is the statement of the rules the conclusion is checked against that\n86\t// review-brief/4 and /5 carry, byte for byte; a version never changes its text.\n87\tconst briefRulesTextV5 = \"POSE checks the conclusion before it records it, and refuses the whole draft when one rule breaks: (a) a `passed` criterion of kind judgment carries a `rationale` saying what you examined and what you concluded; (b) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is exactly one of the refs listed under Sealed evidence (`<class>:<id>`, of a class the criterion asks for when it names one), never a file and line, a command or a structural fact id: those go in a finding or in the `rationale`; (c) a criterion disposed `finding` carries as its `evidence` the `id` of a finding listed in `findings`, and that finding is open until you give it `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; (d) each structural fact listed above is answered by the criterion that asks for structural mapping, as its `mappings`: `[{\\\"delta\\\": <fact id>, \\\"basis\\\": <requirement or decision ref>, \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": <why>}]`, or `not-applicable` with the reason; (e) a `not-applicable` carries a `rationale` and is refused when the bundle seals evidence of a class the criterion asks for; (f) every required criterion and every tool above is answered; (g) the `disposition` of a tool is `passed`, `failed`, `not-used` or `deferred`, never anything else (`not-run` is refused); a tool listed as required must be run and `passed`, with the ref of the sealed evidence it produced as `evidence` when it names classes, and `not-used` is accepted for a required tool only when the plan says no producer exists; a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; (h) the `evidence` of a tool is `<class>:<ref>`: when the tool lists evidence classes, a ref of one of them that the bundle sealed (listed under Sealed evidence), otherwise `command:` followed by the command you ran; a bare command line is refused; (i) a draft that approves leaves no finding open: each finding is either a follow-up with `action`, `owner` and `review_by`, which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes; a finding without them is open and the approval is refused.\"\n88\t\n89\t// briefRulesText is the statement of those rules in the brief of template. review-brief/6 also\n90\t// says which severities the sealed policy lets a follow-up be accepted at, that a tool whose\n91\t// precondition is the completion of the review is answered deferred, the component scoping of\n92\t// evidence, and what a mapping's basis is.\n93\tfunc briefRulesText(template string, bundle ReviewBundle) string {\n94\t\tif template != reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules && template != reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable {\n95\t\t\treturn briefRulesTextV5\n96\t\t}\n97\t\ttext := briefRulesTextV5\n98\t\tseverities := strings.Join(bundle.Payload.SealedGates().AcceptedRiskSeverities, \", \")\n99\t\tif severities == \"\" {\n100\t\t\tseverities = \"none\"\n101\t\t}\n102\t\ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`;\", \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; a required tool whose precondition is the completion of the review (`review-check`, `closeout-check`) cannot pass before your attestation: answer it `deferred` with a `rationale`;\", 1)\n103\t\ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes;\", \"which is recorded as an accepted risk only when its severity is one the sealed review policy accepts (\"+severities+\"), or the draft requests changes and any finding of another severity is fixed first;\", 1)\n104\t\tif template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable {\n105\t\t\ttext += \" (l) a draft that dispenses with every required criterion as `not-applicable` is refused: a scope whose whole plan is inapplicable is not reviewed by it;\"\n106\t\t}\n107\t\treturn text + \" (j) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is of a class the criterion asks for and, when the criterion or tool belongs to a component, of that component (the Sealed evidence list names the module of each ref); (k) the `basis` of a mapping is a requirement or decision id of the scope's spec, such as R1 or D1.\"\n108\t}\n109\t\n110\t// reviewBriefStatesRules reports a template that states the rules the conclusion is\n111\t// checked against.\n112\tfunc reviewBriefStatesRules(template string) bool {\n113\t\treturn template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable || template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || template == reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs || template == reviewBriefTemplateConclusions\n114\t}\n115\t\n116\t// reviewBriefEarlierTemplates are the review templates a run may have been\n117\t// briefed with before the current one, newest first; a run briefed with one\n118\t// is re-rendered with it to verify and to continue (the brief a run was sent\n119\t// never changes under it).\n120\tvar reviewBriefEarlierTemplates = []string{reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules, reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs, reviewBriefTemplateConclusions, reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion, reviewBriefTemplateRounds, reviewBriefTemplateFirst}\n121\t\n122\t// briefEarlierTemplates are, per kind, the templates a run may have been\n123\t// briefed with before the current one, newest first.\n124\tvar briefEarlierTemplates = map[string][]string{\n125\t\tReviewBriefKindReview:       reviewBriefEarlierTemplates,\n126\t\tReviewBriefKindAdjudication: {adjudicationBriefTemplateFirst},\n127\t\tReviewBriefKindSmoke:        {smokeBriefTemplateFirst},\n128\t}\n129\t\n130\t// ReviewBriefKinds lists the accepted kinds.\n131\tfunc ReviewBriefKinds() []string {\n132\t\treturn []string{ReviewBriefKindReview, ReviewBriefKindAdjudication, ReviewBriefKindSmoke}\n133\t}\n134\t\n135\t// RenderReviewBrief renders the brief of kind for target, a bundle id or a\n136\t// scope ref, from its current sealed bundle. A superseded bundle is refused:\n137\t// a brief for it would ask a reviewer to judge content that has moved.\n138\tfunc (s Store) RenderReviewBrief(target, kind string, notes string) (ReviewBrief, error) {\n139\t\treturn s.renderReviewBriefAs(target, kind, notes, \"\")\n140\t}\n141\t\n142\t// RenderReviewBriefMatching renders the brief a run was sent: the current\n143\t// template, or the one before it when that is the one whose digest the run\n144\t// recorded, so a run briefed before the round protocol still verifies and\n145\t// continues.\n146\tfunc (s Store) RenderReviewBriefMatching(target, kind, notes, digest string) (ReviewBrief, error) {\n147\t\tbrief, err := s.renderReviewBriefAs(target, kind, notes, \"\")\n148\t\tif err != nil || brief.Digest == digest {\n149\t\t\treturn brief, err\n150\t\t}\n151\t\tif kind == \"\" {\n152\t\t\tkind = ReviewBriefKindReview\n153\t\t}\n154\t\tfor _, version := range briefEarlierTemplates[kind] {\n155\t\t\tif earlier, eerr := s.renderReviewBriefAs(target, kind, notes, version); eerr == nil && earlier.Digest == digest {\n156\t\t\t\treturn earlier, nil\n157\t\t\t}\n158\t\t}\n159\t\treturn brief, nil\n160\t}\n161\t\n162\tfunc (s Store) renderReviewBriefAs(target, kind, notes, version string) (ReviewBrief, error) {\n163\t\tif kind == \"\" {\n164\t\t\tkind = ReviewBriefKindReview\n165\t\t}\n166\t\ttemplate, ok := reviewBriefTemplates[kind]\n167\t\tif !ok {\n168\t\t\treturn ReviewBrief{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: unknown brief kind %q; kinds: %s\", kind, strings.Join(ReviewBriefKinds(), \", \"))\n169\t\t}\n170\t\tif version != \"\" {\n171\t\t\ttemplate = version\n172\t\t}\n173\t\tvar bundle ReviewBundle\n174\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(target, \"rvb-\") {\n175\t\t\tloaded, err := s.LoadReviewBundle(target)\n176\t\t\tif err != nil {\n177\t\t\t\treturn ReviewBrief{}, err\n178\t\t\t}\n179\t\t\tcurrent, err := s.CurrentReviewBundle(loaded.Payload.Scope.Ref)\n180\t\t\tif err != nil {\n181\t\t\t\treturn ReviewBrief{}, err\n182\t\t\t}\n183\t\t\tif current == nil || current.BundleID != loaded.BundleID {\n184\t\t\t\treturn ReviewBrief{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: bundle %s is superseded by current semantic inputs; seal the scope again and brief the new bundle\", target)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"bdf7092b-f896-46e4-83f5-a5dd1d77d1e2","timestamp":"2026-11-09T15:29:22.706Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1739780139/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go","content":"\tBundleDigest    string `json:\"bundle_digest\"`\n\tDigest          string `json:\"digest\"`\n\tText            string `json:\"text\"`\n}\n\n// The review template that briefs rounds and asks for a pose-draft block\n// (spec pose-delegated-review-round-protocol), and the one before it, kept so\n// a run briefed with it still verifies.\nconst (\n\t// A change to the text of a published version takes a new one (spec\n\t// pose-review-brief-templates-are-immutable). /5 stated how a round after the first\n\t// names the findings it accounts for.\n\treviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs = \"review-brief/5\"\n\t// reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules stated the accepted-risk severities and more, see briefRulesText.\n\treviewBriefTemplateRiskRules = \"review-brief/6\"\n\t// reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable is the current template: it also says that a draft\n\t// cannot dispense with every required criterion as not-applicable.\n\treviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable = \"review-brief/7\"\n\t// reviewBriefTemplateConclusions asked for the typed conclusion and stated its rules,\n\t// without the identifiers of the findings of earlier rounds.\n\t// reviewBriefTemplateConclusions (/4) asked for the typed conclusion and stated the rules\n\t// the engine checks before it records one (spec pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules).\n\treviewBriefTemplateConclusions = \"review-brief/4\"\n\t// reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion asked for the conclusion without stating\n\t// those rules; kept so a run briefed with it still verifies and concludes.\n\treviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion = \"review-brief/3\"\n\treviewBriefTemplateRounds          = \"review-brief/2\"\n\treviewBriefTemplateFirst           = \"review-brief/1\"\n)\n\n// reviewBriefAsksConclusion reports a template that asks for the typed conclusion.\nfunc reviewBriefAsksConclusion(template string) bool {\n\treturn template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable || template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || template == reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs || template == reviewBriefTemplateConclusions || template == reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion\n}\n\n// briefRulesTextV5 is the statement of the rules the conclusion is checked against that\n// review-brief/4 and /5 carry, byte for byte; a version never changes its text.\nconst briefRulesTextV5 = \"POSE checks the conclusion before it records it, and refuses the whole draft when one rule breaks: (a) a `passed` criterion of kind judgment carries a `rationale` saying what you examined and what you concluded; (b) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is exactly one of the refs listed under Sealed evidence (`<class>:<id>`, of a class the criterion asks for when it names one), never a file and line, a command or a structural fact id: those go in a finding or in the `rationale`; (c) a criterion disposed `finding` carries as its `evidence` the `id` of a finding listed in `findings`, and that finding is open until you give it `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; (d) each structural fact listed above is answered by the criterion that asks for structural mapping, as its `mappings`: `[{\\\"delta\\\": <fact id>, \\\"basis\\\": <requirement or decision ref>, \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": <why>}]`, or `not-applicable` with the reason; (e) a `not-applicable` carries a `rationale` and is refused when the bundle seals evidence of a class the criterion asks for; (f) every required criterion and every tool above is answered; (g) the `disposition` of a tool is `passed`, `failed`, `not-used` or `deferred`, never anything else (`not-run` is refused); a tool listed as required must be run and `passed`, with the ref of the sealed evidence it produced as `evidence` when it names classes, and `not-used` is accepted for a required tool only when the plan says no producer exists; a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; (h) the `evidence` of a tool is `<class>:<ref>`: when the tool lists evidence classes, a ref of one of them that the bundle sealed (listed under Sealed evidence), otherwise `command:` followed by the command you ran; a bare command line is refused; (i) a draft that approves leaves no finding open: each finding is either a follow-up with `action`, `owner` and `review_by`, which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes; a finding without them is open and the approval is refused.\"\n\n// briefRulesText is the statement of those rules in the brief of template. review-brief/6 also\n// says which severities the sealed policy lets a follow-up be accepted at, that a tool whose\n// precondition is the completion of the review is answered deferred, the component scoping of\n// evidence, and what a mapping's basis is.\nfunc briefRulesText(template string, bundle ReviewBundle) string {\n\tif template != reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules && template != reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable {\n\t\treturn briefRulesTextV5\n\t}\n\ttext := briefRulesTextV5\n\tseverities := strings.Join(bundle.Payload.SealedGates().AcceptedRiskSeverities, \", \")\n\tif severities == \"\" {\n\t\tseverities = \"none\"\n\t}\n\ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`;\", \"a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; a required tool whose precondition is the completion of the review (`review-check`, `closeout-check`) cannot pass before your attestation: answer it `deferred` with a `rationale`;\", 1)\n\ttext = strings.Replace(text, \"which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes;\", \"which is recorded as an accepted risk only when its severity is one the sealed review policy accepts (\"+severities+\"), or the draft requests changes and any finding of another severity is fixed first;\", 1)\n\tif template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable {\n\t\ttext += \" (l) a draft that dispenses with every required criterion as `not-applicable` is refused: a scope whose whole plan is inapplicable is not reviewed by it;\"\n\t}\n\treturn text + \" (j) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is of a class the criterion asks for and, when the criterion or tool belongs to a component, of that component (the Sealed evidence list names the module of each ref); (k) the `basis` of a mapping is a requirement or decision id of the scope's spec, such as R1 or D1.\"\n}\n\n// reviewBriefStatesRules reports a template that states the rules the conclusion is\n// checked against.\nfunc reviewBriefStatesRules(template string) bool {\n\treturn template == reviewBriefTemplateAllNotApplicable || template == reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules || template == reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs || template == reviewBriefTemplateConclusions\n}\n\n// reviewBriefEarlierTemplates are the review templates a run may have been\n// briefed with before the current one, newest first; a run briefed with one\n// is re-rendered with it to verify and to continue (the brief a run was sent\n// never changes under it).\nvar reviewBriefEarlierTemplates = []string{reviewBriefTemplateRiskRules, reviewBriefTemplateRoundIDs, reviewBriefTemplateConclusions, reviewBriefTemplateTypedConclusion, reviewBriefTemplateRounds, reviewBriefTemplateFirst}\n\n// briefEarlierTemplates are, per kind, the templates a run may have been\n// briefed with before the current one, newest first.\nvar briefEarlierTemplates = map[string][]string{\n\tReviewBriefKindReview:       reviewBriefEarlierTemplates,\n\tReviewBriefKindAdjudication: {adjudicationBriefTemplateFirst},\n\tReviewBriefKindSmoke:        {smokeBriefTemplateFirst},\n}\n\n// ReviewBriefKinds lists the accepted kinds.\nfunc ReviewBriefKinds() []string {\n\treturn []string{ReviewBriefKindReview, ReviewBriefKindAdjudication, ReviewBriefKindSmoke}\n}\n\n// RenderReviewBrief renders the brief of kind for target, a bundle id or a\n// scope ref, from its current sealed bundle. A superseded bundle is refused:\n// a brief for it would ask a reviewer to judge content that has moved.\nfunc (s Store) RenderReviewBrief(target, kind string, notes string) (ReviewBrief, error) {\n\treturn s.renderReviewBriefAs(target, kind, notes, \"\")\n}\n\n// RenderReviewBriefMatching renders the brief a run was sent: the current\n// template, or the one before it when that is the one whose digest the run\n// recorded, so a run briefed before the round protocol still verifies and\n// continues.\nfunc (s Store) RenderReviewBriefMatching(target, kind, notes, digest string) (ReviewBrief, error) {\n\tbrief, err := s.renderReviewBriefAs(target, kind, notes, \"\")\n\tif err != nil || brief.Digest == digest {\n\t\treturn brief, err\n\t}\n\tif kind == \"\" {\n\t\tkind = ReviewBriefKindReview\n\t}\n\tfor _, version := range briefEarlierTemplates[kind] {\n\t\tif earlier, eerr := s.renderReviewBriefAs(target, kind, notes, version); eerr == nil && earlier.Digest == digest {\n\t\t\treturn earlier, nil\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn brief, nil\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) renderReviewBriefAs(target, kind, notes, version string) (ReviewBrief, error) {\n\tif kind == \"\" {\n\t\tkind = ReviewBriefKindReview\n\t}\n\ttemplate, ok := reviewBriefTemplates[kind]\n\tif !ok {\n\t\treturn ReviewBrief{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: unknown brief kind %q; kinds: %s\", kind, strings.Join(ReviewBriefKinds(), \", \"))\n\t}\n\tif version != \"\" {\n\t\ttemplate = version\n\t}\n\tvar bundle ReviewBundle\n\tif strings.HasPrefix(target, \"rvb-\") {\n\t\tloaded, err := s.LoadReviewBundle(target)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn ReviewBrief{}, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tcurrent, err := s.CurrentReviewBundle(loaded.Payload.Scope.Ref)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn ReviewBrief{}, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif current == nil || current.BundleID != loaded.BundleID {\n\t\t\treturn ReviewBrief{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: bundle %s is superseded by current semantic inputs; seal the scope again and brief the new bundle\", target)","numLines":135,"startLine":50,"totalLines":520}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0119XmyQEHa4nCmzon2rFokX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
