{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsbMkbtzXaY6gB4XDsyF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm **approving**. The change does what the spec asks; I found six low-severity defects, filed as follow-ups that can be accepted as risks.\n\nI couldn't run `go test`, `git log` or `git diff` because the profile doesn't allow them. Test results therefore come from the sealed evidence plus my reading of the test code. I ran the two tools the profile allows, and both passed: `artifact-check` reported 913 orphan warnings across the repository but none in this scope's files, and `surface-check` reported 0 findings.\n\n**Prior round-3 findings, checked:**\n- **P1 is fixed:** the brief now states rule (l) at `review_brief.go:105`, and the tie test maps its message at `review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go:52`.\n- **P6 is fixed:** the decision-line exception now replaces the last occurrence (`review_brief.go:486`).\n- **P4 is fixed:** the spec's Security text is corrected (spec line 54).\n- **P3 and P5 are not fully fixed:** two stale references remain (Q2, Q3).\n- **P2:** I didn't check the manual's wording on accepted-risk severities; I only grepped it for the template name.\n\nThis brief is round 1 of a new bundle and has no `prior_findings` field, so I name the earlier findings only here.\n\n**Unresolved assumption:** `artifact-check` reports change set `cs-e8be018aeadf` with head `1b53be73`, but the bundle names `cs-f60393635451` with head `c863f9c3`. I couldn't check this: `git log` isn't allowed and the worktree's HEAD file is outside my read scope. The tree does contain the `/7` content.\n\n## Criteria\n| criterion | disposition | evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration` |\n| backend-concurrency | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\n| backend-contracts | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration` |\n| backend-input-errors | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration` |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration` |\n| backend-observability | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration` |\n| compatibility | finding | Q1 |\n| correctness | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration` |\n| design-causality | passed | `structure:design-cba9a2b04088cab0` |\n| documentation | finding | Q2 |\n| operability | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration` |\n| requirements | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration` |\n| scope | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/artifact-claim-boundary-integration` |\n| security | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration` |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration` |\n\n## Structural facts\n- **SD-2ca2036f** (`validation-matrix.json`) maps to R2. The new check `review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration` runs the tie test and the other traced tests.\n- **SD-fb956636** (`delegation.json`) maps to D2 (R4). The Claude reviewer profile's allow-list is in all three commands (`delegation.json:147,183,206`).\n\n## Defects (all low, follow-up)\n- **Q1, `review_brief.go:483-488`:** the P6 fix also changes how `review-brief/6` renders when the notes contain \"Everything outside the block is yours and is not read.\"\n  - Going by the implementer's P6 note, `/6` used to replace the first occurrence and now replaces the last. I couldn't diff the old code to confirm.\n  - The golden digest fixture has no such notes, so nothing would catch the change.\n  - For that input, `/6` no longer renders as it did, which breaks the \"a version never changes its text\" claim.\n- **Q2, spec line 58:** \"New runs are briefed with `/4`\" is stale; R3 makes `/7` current.\n- **Q3, `review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go`:** three problems in the R4 and R3 tests:\n  - Line 50: the comment says \"current template is /6\".\n  - Line 113: the test doesn't require `Bash(git ls-files:*)`, which R4 names.\n  - Lines 80 and 96: the test skips silently when the policy or the profile is missing.\n- **Q4, `review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go:98`:** the extraction ignores string literals shorter than 14 characters and messages built from non-literal values. A short new blocker could get past R2.\n- **Q5, `review_brief.go:105-107` and `:68-71`:** the brief lists rule (l) between (i) and (j), and two comments on `reviewBriefTemplateConclusions` duplicate and contradict each other.\n- **Q6, `review_conclusions.go:211`:** the comment still says the conclusion template is `review-brief/3`, though `/3` to `/7` now ask for one. This may predate the change.\n\ndecision: approved\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"Q1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\", \"line\": 483, \"summary\": \"The P6 last-occurrence replacement also applies to review-brief/6, so /6 renders differently than before when the notes contain the sentence; the golden digest fixture has no such notes and cannot catch it\", \"action\": \"Keep the earlier replacement for /6 and apply the last-occurrence one only from /7, or add a golden fixture whose notes contain the sentence\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules.md\", \"line\": 58, \"summary\": \"Compatibility says new runs are briefed with /4; R3 makes /7 current\", \"action\": \"Correct the line to /7 at closeout\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\", \"line\": 113, \"summary\": \"The R4 test does not require Bash(git ls-files:*), skips silently when the policy or profile is missing (lines 80 and 96), and the comment at line 50 says the current template is /6\", \"action\": \"Require git ls-files, fail instead of skipping in this repository, and fix the comment\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go\", \"line\": 98, \"summary\": \"Fragment extraction ignores literals under 14 characters and non-literal messages, so a short new blocker could escape the R2 tie\", \"action\": \"Take every string literal passed to the blockers append or Errorf calls, whatever its length, or list the ignored ones explicitly\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\", \"line\": 105, \"summary\": \"The brief renders rule (l) between (i) and (j); the comments at lines 68-71 on reviewBriefTemplateConclusions duplicate and contradict each other\", \"action\": \"Order the rule letters in the next template version and merge the comments\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q6\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\", \"line\": 211, \"summary\": \"The comment names review-brief/3 as the conclusion template; /3 to /7 now ask for one\", \"action\": \"Update the comment to name reviewBriefAsksConclusion\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the implementer's notes against the code. Verified: rule (l) at review_brief.go:105 and its tie at review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go:52; LastIndex at review_brief.go:486; the profile allow-list at delegation.json:147,183,206; no preflight rule changed (the rule-l message is at review_bundle.go:3874, a file outside the change). Accepted risks: Q1-Q6 (low). Unresolved: artifact-check reports change set cs-e8be018aeadf with head 1b53be73 while the bundle names cs-f60393635451 with head c863f9c3; the profile allows no git log, so this was not resolved.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"The change is pure string rendering and a static policy; it adds no shared state or goroutine. The matrix check runs with -race.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The golden digests pin /1 to /7 (testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json); RenderReviewBriefMatching walks the earlier templates (review_brief.go:120,146-160).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The brief now states the refusal messages, which are mapped by the tie test.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\", \"rationale\": \"reviewBriefAsksConclusion covers /3 to /7 (review_brief.go:81-83) and review_conclusions.go:216 consumes it.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The refusal messages are unchanged and named; the brief maps each one to a sentence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"Q1\", \"rationale\": \"Runs briefed with /3 to /6 are re-rendered by version and their digests are pinned; Q1 is a latent /6 rendering change that occurs only when the notes contain the replaced sentence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Read briefRulesText and renderReviewBriefBody: (l) is appended only for /7; the /6 severities are read from the sealed policy; the rendered brief of this run shows rules (a) to (l).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-cba9a2b04088cab0\", \"rationale\": \"D1 states the rules in a new template version because the brief, not the notes, reaches every run; D2 widens the profile to the plan tools only. Examined the spec decisions and the two structural facts.\", \"mappings\": [\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-2ca2036f\", \"basis\": \"R2\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The validation matrix gains review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration, which runs the tie test and the traced R1-R4 tests\"},\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-fb956636\", \"basis\": \"D2\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"delegation.json gives the Claude reviewer profile the R4 allow-list in all three of its commands\"}\n    ]},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"Q2\", \"rationale\": \"POSE.md:1063 and pt-BR POSE.md:1060 name /7; scaffold parity is sealed; the spec still says /4 at line 58.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the brief text and the preflight messages: each rule is stated in actionable terms and the refusal names the broken rule.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Each of R1-R5 is traced to a test the matrix check runs; the R4 test gap is Q3.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/artifact-claim-boundary-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The 15 changed files plus the spec match the spec's artifact list exactly; the non-goals hold (no preflight rule changed, no write verb allowed).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The allow-list is limited to git status, git ls-files and the four plan tools; my own compound commands were refused in this run, and the spec claims no filesystem containment.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Compared with the minimal option (notes per run): the template version is the existing mechanism and adds no file. The choice is invalidated when a draft that follows the brief is refused by an unstated rule (the low follow-up in the spec).\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-brief-states-the-conclusion-rules --strict\", \"rationale\": \"No errors; the 913 findings are repo-wide orphan warnings, none in this scope\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"The profile does not allow pose assess; the sealed structure:design-cba9a2b04088cab0 was read instead\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"The profile does not allow pose assess\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"The profile does not allow pose assess\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"The profile does not allow pose assess\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completed review\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completed review\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Not in the profile's allow-list\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Also run here: surface.findings=0, 198 results, 1 target\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\", \"rationale\": \"The profile does not allow pose validate; the sealed strict validation produced this evidence\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"The profile does not allow pose validate; the sealed strict validation of pose-mcp produced this evidence\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":53318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"0aad23dc-6224-40ab-af12-ce713b402846","timestamp":"202